domain Cc304Revision5TimePolicyCorrection:
  description "Remove superseded time semantics without selecting undecided production values."
evidence E1:
  "Accepted implementation-design revision 5 defines provider transport timeout and worker lease as separate explicitly identified policies with no design default and forbids a whole-attempt semantic deadline."
evidence E2:
  "Before this correction, SemanticAuthoringPolicyV1 and its runtime fixed a 240000 millisecond whole-attempt deadline and a 60000 millisecond provider timeout."
evidence E3:
  "The corrected runtime removes elapsed time from cumulative admission and orchestration termination, takes provider timeout only from ProviderTransportPolicyV1, and passes WorkerExecutionPolicyV1 lease duration through focused claim, renewal, and heartbeat."
evidence E4:
  "Focused environment configuration now requires both policy identities, route or platform identities, and positive safe-integer durations; the focused worker rejects missing policy before claim."
evidence E5:
  "Same-run transport recovery is not implemented, so selecting one recovery fails closed instead of pretending conformance."
evidence E6:
  "Controlled semantic authoring, focused owner-worker, and authoring job suites pass 82 of 82 tests; shared, backend, frontend, and deployment typechecks pass."
premise P1:
  "Controlled fixture durations are test inputs and do not establish production policy values."
premise P2:
  "The legacy family-authoring default remains for legacy routes, while configured focused execution cannot inherit it implicitly."
pending U1:
  "Exact production timeout, worker lease, and zero-or-one recovery policy remain unselected and require later evidence and owner acceptance."
pending U2:
  "Transport and worker policy identities are explicit runtime configuration but are not yet persisted as independent fields in SemanticAuthoringRunV1."
decision D1 based_on E1, E2, E3, E4, E5, E6, P1, P2, U1, U2:
  "Retain this as a local cc304 source correction. Do not activate or deploy it, do not claim complete Revision 5 recovery conformance, and next persist the independently frozen policy identities before implementing optional same-run recovery."
